# JOURNAL / EXEcute: record a session to a .jou file, then replay it (cmdref: Session & Files)
# JOUrnal toggles recording (READ_LOH journals per token: prompt answers included);
# EXEcute (also LQW) replays a .jou through the command stack (give the STEM: .jou is appended, as JOUrnal does).  The replay must
# re-run the load and the OPD and print a second RMS line.  The /null answers the
# plot-device prompt (the first OPD of a session asks); the replay re-asks and the
# journal carries the answer.
# COPY: $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/Cassegrain.in
journal
$TMP/rec_session
old $DECK
opd 3
/null
journal
exe
$TMP/rec_session
# EXPECT: Writing journal file .*rec_session\.jou
# EXPECT: Closing journal file \S*rec_session\.jou\.
# (pre-fix the closing line printed stack garbage: JOU_LOH's file name was not SAVEd)
# EXPECT: Reading from journal file
# EXPECT: (RMS OPD error is[\s\S]*){2}
# EXPECT-NOT: Couldn't find journal file
